Not necessarily, with good stats and equipment. Even in the worst case -
orcish - with maxed Int, a +5 HoB, and a robe, there is a non-zero chance
of casting identify even at XL 1 (obviously you won't have all that - or
enough mana - but it illustrates that spells can have worthwhile yields
for any character; get the right kit together, scum those fountains, and
you will be able to cast the most useful utility spell in the game).

By XL 14, which you must reach, there's a 37% chance on identify - more
than good enough to identify quite a bit of stuff with each mana recharge.
At XL 15 the chance of Magic Mapping becomes non-zero; at XL 18 identify
works more than half the time, and at 22 it is _100%_ reliable. At XL 30
there's a 26% chance of magic mapping working; a barbarian with maxed XL
won't regret that.

The situation is much better for a human barbarian, who by Quest level has
a 49% chance with identify, and whose chance on mapping caps out at 26%.

Yes, the very high level spells are not readily available, but there's a
lot of good stuff in levels 1-3. _Charm monster_ is level 3.

>But the little mana
>he has does not make spellcasting an interesting option,

He'll have more mana if he scums for stat raises from magic fountains. :-)
